  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "J. Ratnesh Nagar vs State Of Maharashtra on 22 June, 2022 Author: Bharati Dangre Bench: Bharati Dangre 1/4 20 Aba 1588-22.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1588 Of 2022 J. Ratnesh Nagar .. Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra .. Respondent With Anticipatory Bail Application No.1587 Of 2022 Dinesh @ Raju Lalman Gupta .. Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra .. Respondent ... Mr.Harshad Sathe i/b Saurabh Butala for the applicants. Mrs.A.A.Takalkar, App for the State. Pi Shri Rahul Rakh from Crime Branch present. Coram: Bharati Dangre, J. Dated : 22nd June, 2022 P.C:- 1 Heard learned counsel for the applicants and learned App for the State.",
    "facts": "3 On 27/4/2022, on a secret information being received to the effect that prohibited substance in form of Gutka, pan masala, scented tobacco, and mixture of betel nut was being transported. A raid was conducted and some white bags were recovered from the back seat of the rickshaw. The said bags contained the prohibited substance and the rickshaw driver as well as the persons accompanying him were brought to the police station. The prohibited substance was found to be worth Rs.37,800/- (SHK Gutka) Rs.23,700/- (Vimal Gutka) and Tobacco worth Rs.2,640/-. Some other accused persons were arrested and in remand report, the name of the applicants were surfaced as supplier of the prohibited substance. That is how they are named as accused in the C.R. 4 Barring the offence u/s.328 of the IPC, all other offences are bailable. The position of law whether an offence u/s.328 gets attracted when the prohibited substance, is transported or supplied, but it is caused to be consumed is attracted or not, till date, is not crystallized. However, in SLP No.843/2021 Mohd. Ali Rehman @ Mohammed Ali Abdul Raheman Shaikh Vs. State of Maharashtra , the Hon'ble Apex Court, on 13/11/2021 took note of the pending matter before it, in regards to invocation of Section 328 of the IPC. The Special Leave Petition is directed to be tagged with the Special Leave Petition filed by the State of Maharashtra in case of Anand Chaurasiya (supra).",
    "arguments": "5 Considering the conundrum of the applicability of J. Ratnesh Nagar vs State Of Maharashtra on 22 June, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/93338430/ 2 provisions of Section 328 in a situation like this, and since the issue is pending before the Hon'ble Apex Court, pursuant to the view of the Division Bench of this Court and since judgment of the Division Bench taking a view that it cannot be invoked, has been stayed, the following ad-interim order would serve the purpose of justice for the time being.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "5 Considering the conundrum of the applicability of J. Ratnesh Nagar vs State Of Maharashtra on 22 June, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/93338430/ 2 provisions of Section 328 in a situation like this, and since the issue is pending before the Hon'ble Apex Court, pursuant to the view of the Division Bench of this Court and since judgment of the Division Bench taking a view that it cannot be invoked, has been stayed, the following ad-interim order would serve the purpose of justice for the time being."
  },
